tment of public safety  since 2017  in this incident officer simmons was  armed with a smith and wesson  mp 2.09 millimeter handgun equipped with  a tactical light  the investigation revealed he fired 14  rounds during the incident  the third involved officer is probation  and parole officer garrett dix  he is 28 years old and has been with the  department of public safety since  2019. in this incident officer dix was  armed with a smith and wesson mp  40 caliber handgun equipped with a  tactical light  the investigation has revealed he fired  three rounds during this incident  the fourth officer is probation and  pearl officer  luis villano villanueva he is 28 years  old and has been with the department of  public safety since 2017.  in this incident officer villanueva was  armed with a smith and wesson mp 40  caliber handgun equipped with a tactical  light  and this investigation has revealed he  fired four rounds during the incident  the suspect who will be pictured to my  left is identified as douglas claiborne  he is a 60 year old  white male adult six foot tall and  weighed approximately 177 pounds  the weapons used during this incident  were  a large kitchen knife and a  20 20 hyundai vehicle as a  used as a deadly weapon in this incident  so and as you can see from the photo of  the kitchen knife it was about a foot  long  had he not survived the applicable  charges would be  murder of a protected person robbery  with a deadly weapon  grand larceny auto and felony evading  now i'm going to go into the details of  the officer involved shooting  on tuesday july 27 2021 at approximately  11 19  hours a.m lb mpd officers responded to a  reported carjacking  at sunset boulevard and las vegas  boulevard the victim stated to  office officers that he and a co-worker  were working at a construction site  when the co-worker saw douglas claiborne  sitting in the victim's vehicle  the victim approached his vehicle and  screamed to claiborne to get out of the  car the victim attempted to open the  doors but they were locked  and then claiborne produced a large  kitchen knife and threatened the victim  the vehicle's keys were left inside of  the car  and claiborne was able to start the  vehicle he then drove away  running over the victim's foot claiborne  and the vehicle's description were then  broadcast throughout the valley  at approximately 11 50 a.m nevada  highway patrol  troopers located the stolen hyundai  traveling  northbound on interstate 15 in the area  of the speedway  exit a traffic stop was attempted by nhp  but claiborne did not stop  a pursuit was initiated and the lvmpd  air unit assisted  nhp by monitoring the pursuit from the  air  he continued northbound on i-15 and  eventually made a u-turn  and then headed southbound throughout  the pursuit claiborne exited and  re-entered the freeway  several times each time he was driving  erratically and dangerously through the  community  once back on the freeway claiborne drove  south on i-15  reaching speeds between 35 and  well over 50 miles per hour and continue  driving erratic  stop stick tire deflation devices were  deployed  numerous times yet claiborne was able to  move or  maneuver around them at approximately 12  18 p.m trooper  micah may deployed stop sticks on i-15  near the neon gateway which is by the  charleston  boulevard exit as claiborne approached  the stop sticks  he avoided the stop sticks and  intentionally intentionally drove  directly towards trooper may and struck  him with the stolen vehicle  trooper may then became lodged in the  windshield  of the vehicle as claiborne continued to  drive south on the freeway  several nevada highway patrol troopers  to include trooper della bella  accelerated up to claiborne's vehicle  the stolen vehicle  and rammed it several times the vehicle  was forcibly stopped at i-15 and spring  mountain road  just south of sahara trooper della bella  along with pnp officers  simmons dix villanueva exited their  vehicles  and officers then observed claiborne  grabbing trooper may's  gun this prompted the officers to fire  their weapons  at claiborne claiborne was struck  several times  and he was subsequently pronounced  deceased on scene by medical personnel  troopers on the scene were able to  remove trooper may from the vehicle  and immediately began life-saving  measures  the air unit landed on i-15  and transported trooper may rapidly to  umc  trauma unfortunately  on july 29th 2021 trooper may  succumb to his injuries he is survived  by his wife  and his two children i will now show you  video  from our air unit and some body worn  camera  of the ois incident  this is video of him off the freeway  driving through the  neighborhoods  carry wrong way of travel here crossing  over the uh  for the right side of travel still  northbound fifth through carry  heavy traffic down uh cheyenne he's  going off or right  on the shoulder  over here back towards the i-15  [Music]  and making another u-turn back westbound  cheyenne  looks like he's uh trying to get around  our vehicles now  uh continue once not trying to run  a way of travel 70 miles an hour  traffic's getting a little bit heavier  here he'll be up so  unless they uh smash through your cars  looks like they did  uh by the sideswipes of vehicles there  craig road  okay this is the video of the  termination of the pursuit they're going  to be trying to bench  up short medical please 15 self-centered  that's when the shots were fired  this is body cam video  that that was some body cam video from  one of the troopers that  did not fire the weapon at the time but  we felt that that body cam video  really showed the best image of the  incident  and then this last video you're going to  see will be  our air unit landing on i-15  to transport superman  okay  we believe this is the first time we've  used our air support  helicopter to actually land and rescue a  downed officer  and bring them to umc  so um this concludes my initial briefing  i'm here to answer any questions you may  have about the incident  so i'll take a few questions  anybody okay  thank you very much oh okay  from the set steve hey how you doing hey  from the start to finish when the  stolen vehicle was reported that the  pursuit began  correct to the time trooper was  airlifted  what kind of the total i could throw out  a couple of numbers  the pursuit lasted about 42 minutes  and i think it was approximately 20  minutes from the time of the initial  report till the time it was located but  the pursuit was about uh 10 minutes and  then i think it took us about  from the time the helicopter got there  and was able to land i think it was just  a couple of minutes probably three to  four minutes to to actually make the  landing and get them transported  with the channel eight uh you mentioned  that stop sticks were tried a few  a few times and they didn't we're just  able to drive around them were there  other measures  yes they were used several times uh  during as  you can see from the the map right he  went all the way up i-15  then was driving on and off the freeway  and recklessly all around and  um you know sometimes it's hard to  predict but we try to  identify those areas where it would be  safe to use them and deflate the tires  to kind of slow the pursuit down and  bring it to a safe conclusion  and that's what the officers were doing  and the troopers were doing when they  were out there  it kind of relates to those questions  with speeds of between 35 and 55 miles  an hour  uh according to radio traffic why wasn't  it why  weren't uh more aggressive tactics taken  until uh  trooper may was well i think um  and i can't speak to you know the  highway patrol policy because it was  actually  their pursuit but um i know when law  enforcement right we want to do the the  least dangerous thing we want to protect  the people on the roadway and and and  that  is paramount right the safety of the  public even the safety of the suspect  driving the car  so at that point it initially was a  pursuit within those speed limits so  a lot of times we will follow them and  eventually they'll give up or they'll  run out of gas or  they'll see that we have enough  resources unseen and then they stop  but in this case it didn't happen so  they continued to use the stop sticks to  try to  persuade him to stop and at this point  he did not stop  so about how long was it or i guess what  was the distance between  where trooper was hit and where the car  was ultimately stopped  uh well i can't tell you the exact  distance in feet  but i want to say it was about a mile  maybe a mile and a half  down between the exits  at that point he was the only one there  but earlier they had deployed him in  other spots yeah there was a total of  well six and then the seventh deployment  was the one that  um where trooper may was struck i guess  they're in a variety of places yeah i  don't have the specific places but  i will tell you this is a essentially a  72-hour briefing  we want to be transparent about the  details of the officer-involved shooting  and the death of a dedicated public  servant but this investigation isn't  over  this is just the beginning of it so in  the coming weeks and months  we'll continue to investigate follow-up  and  provide information as is asked  yes  um i can we have to make decisions in  high-stress environments  and i believe the officers i mean i  can't speak for them but i can tell you  right now the information that we have  in the preliminary investigation is  it appeared that trooper may was inside  the vehicle and  out of harm's way he was not struck with  any rounds  when the shots were fired so the  officers that are involved in it have to  make that determination  you know we always identify backdrop and  the scene where we're going to use  deadly force  so those are split-second decisions that  officers have to make in a very  challenging environment  thank you very much i appreciate you all  being here today

